  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Imagine popping into a new world and, instead of a random “18+ only” velvet rope, the door scans your Trust Rank—your actual reputation in the community—like a VIP bouncer who’s watched every meme you’ve ever posted. Good actors who’ve earned those green and purple badges get fast-tracked inside, while brand-new alt accounts and serial griefers bounce back to the public lobby to rethink their life choices. It’d reward players for generosity and good vibes, give creators finer control over who comes in, and spare everyone the awkward “Are you really old enough, or just good with Photoshop?” dance. In short: a trust-based instance system would turn VRChat from a roll-of-the-dice nightclub into a curated hangout where quality beats chaos—no fake IDs required.",
